WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.160
Vincent owns a neighborhood barbershop.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.040
He's well liked, always smiling and a

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.960
pillar in the community. Nothing out of

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.680
the ordinary.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.320
Morning, Shen. Just making my deposit.

00:00:12.902 --> 00:00:14.782
When Shin opens Vincent's account, he

00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:17.502
notices a pattern. Several cash deposits

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:20.062
over the past few weeks. Always just

00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:22.982
under $10,000. Always at different

00:00:22.982 --> 00:00:25.942
branches. A little unusual, but Vincent's

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:26.862
a familiar face.

00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:28.591
I have a lot of clients waiting in line

00:00:28.591 --> 00:00:30.911
right now. He probably just did well this

00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:32.111
month. No big deal.

00:00:32.776 --> 00:00:34.856
But it was a big deal. The money Vincent

00:00:34.856 --> 00:00:37.216
deposited didn't stop at his account. It

00:00:37.216 --> 00:00:39.176
moved quietly into lives that would never

00:00:39.176 --> 00:00:39.896
be the same.

00:00:40.797 --> 00:00:42.477
Maya had been missing for two months.

00:00:44.552 --> 00:00:46.712
Sold across borders. Traded hands.

00:00:46.844 --> 00:00:48.924
The same laundered funds from Vincent's

00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:51.724
deposits helped pay for forged documents

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:53.084
and a smuggler's van.

00:00:56.229 --> 00:00:58.189
Because no one flagged the cache, the

00:00:58.189 --> 00:00:59.269
traffickers stay hidden.

00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:10.039
Rico was 19. The pills that stopped his

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:11.879
heart came from a supply chain funded

00:01:11.879 --> 00:01:13.959
through dirty cash. A portion of that

00:01:13.959 --> 00:01:15.279
money was cleaned through routine

00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:16.679
deposits at the bank.

00:01:19.306 --> 00:01:21.346
His father still can't bear to enter his

00:01:21.346 --> 00:01:22.026
empty room.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.740
In another part of the world, an

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.860
explosive device paid for with funds

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.420
funneled through a shell company leveled

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:32.940
a street.

00:01:37.287 --> 00:01:39.207
Iris, a nurse volunteering at a

00:01:39.207 --> 00:01:40.966
children's clinic, was caught in the

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:41.446
blast.

00:01:48.077 --> 00:01:50.237
The shell company was funded by Vincent's

00:01:50.237 --> 00:01:51.197
Laundering Network.

00:01:52.132 --> 00:01:53.972
Shen doesn't know, but he could have

00:01:53.972 --> 00:01:54.372
acted.

00:01:54.975 --> 00:01:57.775
A report, a note, a raised flag.

00:01:58.335 --> 00:01:59.935
Instead, silence.

00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:02.777
AML isn't just a compliance checkbox.

00:02:02.937 --> 00:02:04.657
It's a shield for our bank, our

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:07.337
community, and the people we serve. After

00:02:07.337 --> 00:02:08.537
all, would you trust your bank if it

00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:09.337
failed to act?

